@SYSTEM_TITLE
; Emuera's WINAPI refusal covers 35 named methods, not every method that
; touches a bitmap. `SpriteStateMethod` (`Creator.Method.cs:5759`, behind
; SPRITECREATED/SPRITEWIDTH/SPRITEHEIGHT/SPRITEPOSX/SPRITEPOSY),
; `SpriteGetColorMethod` (`:5818`) and `SpriteDisposeMethod` (`:6063`) were
; never given the guard, and `CBGClearMethod` (`:6479`) has one that the fork
; commented out (`:6489`, as at `:6532` for CBGCLEARBUTTON, `:6551` for
; CBGREMOVEBMAP, `:6627` for CBGSETCIMG and `:5647` for GROTATE). All of them
; answer in WINAPI mode exactly as they do in GDI+ mode.
; Nothing exists to query here, so these are the "no such sprite" answers: 0
; everywhere and -1 from SPRITEGETCOLOR, whose failure is negative (`:5828`).
PRINTFORML created={SPRITECREATED("nope")}
PRINTFORML width={SPRITEWIDTH("nope")}
PRINTFORML posx={SPRITEPOSX("nope")}
PRINTFORML color={SPRITEGETCOLOR("nope", 0, 0)}
PRINTFORML disposed={SPRITEDISPOSE("nope")}
PRINTFORML cbg={CBGCLEAR()}
